  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">M23 Crisis Response in North Kivu - DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve the socio -sanitary conditions of the populations affected by the crisis by ensuring:  - Access to potable water in Internally Displaced Person (IDP) sites, host communities and health centres;  - Access to adequate, dignified and hygienic sanitation facilities and,  - ensuring a systematic approach to encourage the widespread adoption of safe hygiene practices to keep people and their environment clean through the promotion of hygiene knowledge and practices and community engagement;  - responding to emergency food needs, the acquisition of essential household items, and primary health care coverage by organizing &quot;multi -purpose cash distributions&quot; (food, essential household items, and health);  - Contributing to the adoption of better community protection practices, reducing the risk of violence and abuse, particularly for women, girls, and disproportionately affected groups in the intervention area.</narrative>
  </description>
